---
/**
 * Homepage FAQ: questions about Snugglegum™ Multivitamin and the pre-launch (three versions, flavor
 * vote, sign-up), plus the generic, product-agnostic "gummy supplements" group, which stays
 * brand-neutral so it can answer what/whether/how gummy supplements work. No health claims here.
 */
import FaqGroup from '@/components/home/FaqGroup.astro';
import Brand from '@/components/ui/Brand.astro';

const item = 'border-b-2 border-dashed border-green';
const question = 'flex min-h-12 items-center justify-between gap-5 py-6 text-[clamp(1.15rem,2vw,1.5rem)] font-black uppercase';
const plus = 'faq-plus flex-none text-[26px] font-black';
const answer = 'max-w-[60ch] pb-6 text-[19px] leading-[1.55]';
const badgeClass = 'bg-pink text-ink';
---

<section id="faq" aria-labelledby="faq-heading" class="section-px section-py bg-white text-green">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-[900px]">
    <h2 id="faq-heading" class="display-word stretch-display text-[clamp(2.2rem,5vw,4.25rem)] leading-[0.88]">Questions, answered</h2>

    <div class="mt-[clamp(40px,5vw,64px)] grid gap-[clamp(40px,5vw,64px)]">
      <FaqGroup badgeClass={badgeClass}>
        <span slot="badge">
          <Brand />
        </span>

        <details name="faq-brand" class:list={[item]}>
          <summary class:list={[question]}>
            <span>What is <Brand /> Multivitamin?</span>
            <span aria-hidden="true" class:list={[plus]}>+</span>
          </summary>
          <p class:list={[answer]}><Brand /> Multivitamin is a sugar-free multivitamin gummy with a liquid center that bursts when you bite. It comes in three versions, each with its own formula. It is still in development and not yet available.</p>
        </details>

        <details name="faq-brand" class:list={[item]}>
          <summary class:list={[question]}>
            <span>Which version is for me?</span>
            <span aria-hidden="true" class:list={[plus]}>+</span>
          </summary>
          <p class:list={[answer]}>Pick the one for your age group. Each version is a multivitamin with a formula tailored to the needs of its generation: Gen Z (ages 18 to 29), Millennials (ages 30 to 45) and Boomer (ages 62 to 80). Final formulas and Supplement Facts come at launch.</p>
        </details>

        <details name="faq-brand" class:list={[item]}>
          <summary class:list={[question]}>
            <span>What makes <Brand /> different?</span>
            <span aria-hidden="true" class:list={[plus]}>+</span>
          </summary>
          <p class:list={[answer]}>Poppin’ vitamins you actually want to snack on: sugar-free, with a liquid center that bursts when you bite.</p>
        </details>

        <details name="faq-brand" class:list={[item]}>
          <summary class:list={[question]}>
            <span>What do I get for signing up now?</span>
            <span aria-hidden="true" class:list={[plus]}>+</span>
          </summary>
          <p class:list={[answer]}>The first 500 founding members help pick the first flavor: Pineapple, Energy, or a flavor of your own. You can choose it right in the sign-up form. You confirm your email address once (double opt-in), and you can unsubscribe anytime.</p>
        </details>

        <details name="faq-brand" class:list={[item]}>
          <summary class:list={[question]}>
            <span>When does <Brand /> launch?</span>
            <span aria-hidden="true" class:list={[plus]}>+</span>
          </summary>
          <p class:list={[answer]}>Soon. Join the list and you'll hear first.</p>
        </details>

        <details name="faq-brand" class:list={[item]}>
          <summary class:list={[question]}>
            <span>Where will <Brand /> be available?</span>
            <span aria-hidden="true" class:list={[plus]}>+</span>
          </summary>
          <p class:list={[answer]}>The USA first.</p>
        </details>

        <details name="faq-brand" class:list={[item]}>
          <summary class:list={[question]}>
            <span>Will you spam me?</span>
            <span aria-hidden="true" class:list={[plus]}>+</span>
          </summary>
          <p class:list={[answer]}>No. Launch news and the occasional bad joke. Unsubscribe anytime.</p>
        </details>

        <details name="faq-brand" class:list={[item]}>
          <summary class:list={[question]}>
            <span>What's with the name?</span>
            <span aria-hidden="true" class:list={[plus]}>+</span>
          </summary>
          <p class:list={[answer]}><strong>Snuggle</strong> is the cozy part. <strong>Gum</strong> is how you take it. Put them together and you get <strong><Brand /></strong>.</p>
        </details>
      </FaqGroup>

      <FaqGroup badgeClass={badgeClass}>
        <span slot="badge">About gummy supplements</span>

        <details name="faq-gummies" class:list={[item]}>
          <summary class:list={[question]}>
            <span>What are gummy supplements?</span>
            <span aria-hidden="true" class:list={[plus]}>+</span>
          </summary>
          <p class:list={[answer]}>
            Gummy supplements are chewable dietary supplements made to deliver vitamins, minerals or other functional ingredients
            in a soft, flavored format. They are an alternative to traditional pills, capsules and powders.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details name="faq-gummies" class:list={[item]}>
          <summary class:list={[question]}>
            <span>Do gummy supplements work?</span>
            <span aria-hidden="true" class:list={[plus]}>+</span>
          </summary>
          <p class:list={[answer]}>
            A gummy is simply a delivery format. Whether a gummy provides a meaningful nutritional benefit depends on its
            ingredients, amounts, formulation and quality — not on the fact that it is a gummy.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details name="faq-gummies" class:list={[item]}>
          <summary class:list={[question]}>
            <span>Are gummy vitamins as effective as pills?</span>
            <span aria-hidden="true" class:list={[plus]}>+</span>
          </summary>
          <p class:list={[answer]}>
            They can deliver nutrients effectively, but gummies and pills are not automatically equivalent. Formulation, dosage,
            stability and ingredients matter, so the Supplement Facts panel is more important than the format itself.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details name="faq-gummies" class:list={[item]}>
          <summary class:list={[question]}>
            <span>Are gummy supplements healthy?</span>
            <span aria-hidden="true" class:list={[plus]}>+</span>
          </summary>
          <p class:list={[answer]}>
            That depends on the product. Some gummies contain useful nutrients, while others may contain significant amounts of
            sugar or sugar alcohols. Check the ingredients, serving size and Supplement Facts rather than assuming that every
            gummy is healthy simply because it contains vitamins.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details name="faq-gummies" class:list={[item]}>
          <summary class:list={[question]}>
            <span>Why are supplements made as gummies?</span>
            <span aria-hidden="true" class:list={[plus]}>+</span>
          </summary>
          <p class:list={[answer]}>
            Gummies can be easier and more enjoyable to take than pills, particularly for people who dislike swallowing tablets.
            The trade-off is that gummies have formulation constraints, including taste, texture, stability and the amount of
            active ingredients that can practically be included.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details name="faq-gummies" class:list={[item]}>
          <summary class:list={[question]}>
            <span>Can you take too many gummy supplements?</span>
            <span aria-hidden="true" class:list={[plus]}>+</span>
          </summary>
          <p class:list={[answer]}>
            Yes. Gummies are supplements, not candy, and taking more than the recommended serving can result in excessive
            intake of certain nutrients or ingredients. Always follow the product's recommended serving size.
          </p>
        </details>
      </FaqGroup>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
